# Generated by XcodeGen — regenerate with `xcodegen generate`. project.yml stays
# the reviewable source of truth for the project, the Info.plists and the
# entitlements, but the generated output is committed too: Xcode Cloud builds
# straight from the checkout and never runs XcodeGen, so anything the build
# reads by path has to be in the repo. Edit project.yml, run `xcodegen
# generate`, commit both sides.
#
# Ignore everything inside the project except what a clean checkout must build
# with: the project itself, the shared schemes Xcode Cloud selects a workflow
# from, and the resolved SwiftPM graph. Without that last one Xcode falls back
# to CribWireKit/Package.resolved, which pins only the kit's own dependencies
# and knows nothing of WebRTC or the Tidal SDK, and resolution fails outright
# because Xcode Cloud disables automatic dependency resolution — re-run
# `xcodebuild -resolvePackageDependencies` and commit the result whenever
# `packages:` in project.yml changes.
CribWire.xcodeproj/*
!CribWire.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
!CribWire.xcodeproj/xcshareddata/
!CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/
CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/*
!CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/contents.xcworkspacedata
!CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/
CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/*
!CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/
CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/*
!CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/Package.resolved

# The umbrella workspace is generated as well and holds nothing reviewable.
/CribWire.xcworkspace/

# SwiftPM
.build/
.swiftpm/

# Xcode
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
